2.
Definitions.
- In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
'Captain of Ports' means the Captain of Ports of the Government;
(b)
'channel' means any canal, river, lake, backwaters, creeks or other navigable waterways;
(c)
'ferry' means a place at which goods or passengers or vehicles are conveyed across a channel by means of vessels,
and includes also the approaches to and landing places of a ferry;
(d)
'Government' means the Government of Goa;
(e)
'lessee' means any person who holds right of tolls at public ferry on lease;
(f)
'notification' means a notification published in the Official Gazette;
(g)
'Official Gazette' means the Official Gazette of the Government;
(h)
'prescribed' means prescribed by rules made under this Act;
(i)
'public ferry' means a ferry which is declared to be a public ferry under the provisions of this Act.
